n":{"commit_sha":"b81192a7fc7f8398b4bfd567e7a6f0017ecb5557","position":"1787290550949533001-65bc9268-4667-468d-8539-ed5c3c10d9fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"31aad1773daca281680e422eeacb771aa69d4271db09ee3a6b3bc1fe6ce8a828","event_uuid":"692750a6-d26e-406b-91f5-b61b3d72cb4a","position":{"commit_sha":"d9b0813629048dd04bff73c58c3f1640428c4842","position":"1787290556653746001-692750a6-d26e-406b-91f5-b61b3d72cb4a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7a648c4997a788471a6b65fd2db4277b853bc15dcec529cb4e857dc58546a47d","event_uuid":"85760001-d14f-4392-b705-50e60a9a1f9a","position":{"commit_sha":"cabf31247a9b8c069a3451064b3aa34d91b6feec","position":"1787290562261433001-85760001-d14f-4392-b705-50e60a9a1f9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787290338813130001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3d5dce7f-0eb2-4daf-817f-a9e3f77b4335","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"438a-e1d9-29d3-4081"},{"link_uuid":"17cd52b1-99c0-4d00-b35b-bb64c8a585a0","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c"},{"link_uuid":"a6ca64d5-0ecb-4a04-ae06-159887da5f9f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1515-bebc-0d91-476b"},{"link_uuid":"24e321bb-8539-40da-846b-b5d4d42ee82e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a881-2d9a-16bf-4acb"},{"link_uuid":"65bc9268-4667-468d-8539-ed5c3c10d9fd","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d458-bb1e-cc63-42a6"},{"link_uuid":"692750a6-d26e-406b-91f5-b61b3d72cb4a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2c66-205d-92e1-4419"},{"link_uuid":"85760001-d14f-4392-b705-50e60a9a1f9a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7"}],"description":"# Documentation + portability: mapping seam, provider-neutral reuse, migration safety\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe mapping seam (S1–S8) adds a new config surface, new echo-safe behaviors (breadcrumb,\nreplay), and a new probe command. Operators and future integrators need authoritative docs,\nand the plan-review `project.portability` criterion requires that no capability's only\ntrigger is a specific CI provider — the seam must work across environments with diverse or\nno CI. This child closes the documentation and portability story: it documents the seam end\nto end, records the provider-neutral reuse contract for future Linear/GitLab/GitHub-Issues\nintegrations, and states the migration/rollback story (the feature is additive — an absent\n`[tool.rebar.mapping]` section reproduces today's hardcoded behavior exactly).\n\n## Approach\n\nAuthor docs across the surfaces the seam touches:\n- `docs/config.md` — the `[tool.rebar.mapping]` reserved section reference (extends S1's\n  leaf doc): full axis catalog, the three-layer merge, per-project keying, fail-closed\n  validation, and the orthogonality to `.bridge_state/projects.json`.\n- A mapping-seam guide (new `docs/mapping-seam.md`, indexed in `docs/README.md`) covering\n  the provider-neutral core vs Jira-adapter split, the capability descriptor, the\n  skip/drift/collapse decision paths, transition replay, the parent breadcrumb, and the\n  probe workflow — with the explicit statement that the neutral core is the reuse seam for\n  future targets (Linear/GitLab/GitHub-Issues) whose direct support is out of scope now.\n- `CHANGELOG`/migration note — additive, backward-compatible: absent section = current\n  behavior; no store migration; rollback = delete the section.\n- Portability statement: every mapping behavior is exercised by in-process unit tests with\n  injected transports (no live Jira, no specific CI required); the only live touchpoint\n  (the probe) degrades to an offline emit and is never a CI gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/config.md`, `docs/mapping-seam.md` (new), `docs/README.md` (index entry).\n- A migration/rollback note in the repo's changelog surface.\n- No source-code change (docs-only child) — file-impact is the doc paths.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocs-only child: no automated test tier. Verification is by review against the acceptance\ncriteria (the plan-review gate defers testing on a docs child to a reviewer-checkable\noutcome). The portability *claim* it documents is substantiated by the unit suites in\nS1–S8 (each names an injected-transport, no-live-Jira tier); this child asserts those exist\nand are referenced, it does not add new behavior to test.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` documents the full `[tool.rebar.mapping]` axis catalog, merge\n  layers, and per-project keying — verified by reviewer check that each axis (status, type,\n  link, priority, create_defaults) and the merge order appear.\n- [ ] `docs/mapping-seam.md` exists, is indexed in `docs/README.md`, and states the\n  provider-neutral core as the reuse seam for future targets — verified by reviewer check\n  for the index entry and the reuse statement.\n- [ ] The migration note states the feature is additive with an absent-section = current-\n  behavior guarantee and a delete-the-section rollback — verified by reviewer check.\n- [ ] The portability statement records that every mapping behavior is covered by\n  injected-transport unit tests requiring no live Jira and no specific CI provider —\n  verified by reviewer check against the S1–S8 test sections.\n\nTest tier: **none (docs-only)** — the mechanism is documentation; the observable oracle is\nreviewer verification against the four criteria above, which is the correct tier for a\nchild that adds no runtime behavior.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"mapping section reference"},{"path":"docs/mapping-seam.md","reason":"new mapping-seam guide"},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"index the new guide"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","1515-bebc-0d91-476b"],["depends_on","2c66-205d-92e1-4419"],["depends_on","438a-e1d9-29d3-4081"],["depends_on","a881-2d9a-16bf-4acb"],["depends_on","a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c"],["depends_on","ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7"],["depends_on","d458-bb1e-cc63-42a6"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"14f4-d616-70df-466d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Documentation + portability: mapping seam, provider-neutral reuse, migration safety","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["af718ae8-d361-4af6-b40d-26a93eee3f3e","3fb7835d-307e-4b8a-864d-88a48cf2235c","3d5dce7f-0eb2-4daf-817f-a9e3f77b4335","17cd52b1-99c0-4d00-b35b-bb64c8a585a0","a6ca64d5-0ecb-4a04-ae06-159887da5f9f","24e321bb-8539-40da-846b-b5d4d42ee82e","65bc9268-4667-468d-8539-ed5c3c10d9fd","692750a6-d26e-406b-91f5-b61b3d72cb4a","85760001-d14f-4392-b705-50e60a9a1f9a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787296877702817001,"uuid":"d2f60749-a2b3-48e6-becf-f487baf7b28d"}